      "extra": {
        "DestRoleTags": [
          {
            "key": "usageNote-en",
            "note": "NOTE$ea_notes=In almost all jurisdictions, Legal Entities must register a public address. This may or may not be the actual address at which the Legal Entity does its business, it is commonly the address of their lawyer or accountant, but it is the address to which formal communications can be sent. The registered address property points to the Address of the Registered Site. This property can be seen as a shorthand for this property path.",
